# Shell scripts in scripts/ are executed on the Linux VPS. Git on Windows
# normally checks files out with CRLF, and bash treats a trailing \r as part of
# the command, so a CRLF checkout fails with "command not found" on names that
# look correct on screen. Force LF for anything that runs server side.
*.sh text eol=lf

# nginx and Apache config fragments are read by servers on Linux too.
*.conf text eol=lf
.htaccess text eol=lf

# Deliberately no `* text=auto` rule. Adding one to a repo this far along makes
# Git re-examine every tracked file and can produce a large whitespace-only
# diff. The targeted rules above are what actually matter, because those are
# the files that get executed or parsed on the Linux VPS.
